36	 * was wrong. On timeout this DOES throw, which fails the job and tells the
37	 * customer the start failed, even when the process goes on to come up fine a
38	 * moment later (real incident: a Terraria customer's start kept "failing"
39	 * while the server was actually booting normally — world load + "Settling
