commit 1c332f7504a2817e8840bcc9cf1a99b93a85af70
Author: Nxeon <haxkodi@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 00:36:28 2026 +0000

    Power controls: stop spam-clicking (VPS + game) and make the one-job-per-server guard atomic

    Real customer report (Terraria): customers didn't understand that
    Start/Stop/Restart take real time and kept clicking. The buttons just faded
    with no explanation, the status pill stayed "Offline" for the minutes a big
    world takes to load, and the buttons silently came back when the job ended.

    Backend: serverAction and gamePower enforced "one in-flight job per server"
    as count() then create(). Reproduced on staging with a captured Server Action
    request fired 10x concurrently: 3 REBOOT jobs and 2 GAME_POWER jobs for one
    server. New lib/job-guard.ts withServerJobLock runs check + enqueue under a
    per-server pg_advisory_xact_lock. Both actions now return the new job id.

    UI: lib/power-state.ts builds a snapshot from the page's real Job rows;
    components/customer/power/usePowerGuard.ts locks synchronously on click,
    follows the returned job through the page's existing AutoRefresh data (never a
    local timer), adopts a job already in flight on page load, reports how it
    ended and applies a 5s cooldown. PowerStatusNote shows the in-flight action
    with real elapsed time and worker attempt count (no fake progress). Wired into
    VpsHero/VpsPowerControls and GameHero; admin PowerActions now stays disabled
    while any job is in flight (no cooldown for staff).

    Docs: DOCUMENTATION.md changelog + server-lifecycle and game-control
    sections; ROADMAP.md.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

